Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: apq8053-lenovo: preserve simplefb clocks

lk2nd can hand over an actively scanning framebuffer, but the dynamically
created simple-framebuffer node does not describe its clocks. Unused-clock
cleanup therefore gates the display pipeline before the native DRM driver
takes ownership.

On the ThinkSmart View this is associated with poor execution throughput
across all CPU cores and an FT8201 identity-read failure. Keeping only the
display clocks referenced by simplefb restores normal startup throughput,
without disabling clock cleanup globally.

Provide a disabled framebuffer template with the display pipeline's clock
references. lk2nd reuses this node, supplies its relocated memory and mode
information, and enables it. The simplefb driver releases the clock
references when DRM removes the firmware framebuffer.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Base-commit: 7213855948c70fd165356526f1de1c3b6bf4d554
Apply in filename order within this project.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
@@ -25,6 +25,21 @@
 	qcom,msm-id = <QCOM_ID_APQ8053 0>;
 	qcom,board-id = <0x1010520 0>;
 
+	chosen {
+		/* lk2nd supplies the framebuffer geometry before enabling this node. */
+		framebuffer {
+			compatible = "simple-framebuffer";
+			clocks = <&gcc GCC_MDSS_AHB_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_AXI_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_VSYNC_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_MDP_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_BYTE0_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_PCLK0_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_ESC0_CLK>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+	};
+
 	/* Define mmc aliases so they stay the same across boots */
 	aliases {
 		mmc0 = &sdhc_1;
